## UI/UX Development Patterns

### Frontend State Management

**URL State + localStorage Pattern:**
- Use URL parameters as primary source of truth for navigation state (book, chapter, position)
- Fall back to localStorage for persistence across sessions
- Clear URL parameters when returning to library/home view
- Update URL on state changes to enable bookmarking and sharing

**Example Pattern:**
```javascript
// Initialize from URL first, then localStorage
const urlParams = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);
const bookId = urlParams.get('book') || localStorage.getItem('bookId');

// Save state to both URL and localStorage
window.history.pushState({}, '', `?book=${bookId}&chapter=${chapter}`);
localStorage.setItem('bookId', bookId);
```

### Polling & Real-Time Updates

**Smart Polling Strategy:**
- Poll at appropriate intervals (1-3 seconds for active jobs, longer for passive updates)
- Automatically stop polling when conditions are met (all jobs complete, no active work)
- Always clear intervals on component unmount or view changes
- Use separate intervals for different concerns (jobs, chunks, progress)

**Best Practices:**
- Store interval IDs in class properties for cleanup
- Check if interval exists before clearing (avoid errors)
- Stop polling when user navigates away from relevant view
- Resume polling when returning to view if conditions warrant

**Example:**
```javascript
// Start polling
this.jobPollInterval = setInterval(() => {
    this.loadJobs();
    if (this.allJobsComplete()) {
        clearInterval(this.jobPollInterval);
        this.jobPollInterval = null;
    }
}, 1000);

// Cleanup
if (this.jobPollInterval) {
    clearInterval(this.jobPollInterval);
    this.jobPollInterval = null;
}
```

### Modal/Panel Lifecycle Management

**Single Active Modal Pattern:**
- Only one modal/panel visible at a time
- Hide all other modals before showing new one
- Remove dynamically created panels from DOM when closed (prevent accumulation)
- Use event delegation for click-outside-to-close (prevents stopPropagation issues)

**Cleanup Requirements:**
- Remove event listeners when panels are closed
- Clear any polling intervals associated with panel
- Reset form state if applicable
- Remove DOM elements for dynamically created panels

### UI Design Preferences

**Visual Design:**
- Prefer dark mode with glassmorphic effects (backdrop-filter, transparency)
- Use icon libraries (Lucide, Font Awesome) over emojis for consistency
- Implement smooth transitions and hover states
- Use consistent color schemes with CSS variables

**Accessibility:**
- Provide keyboard shortcuts for common actions
- Ensure proper focus management in modals
- Use semantic HTML elements
- Include ARIA labels where appropriate

---

## Background Job Management

### Job Queue Architecture

**Separate Queues by Resource Type:**
- Maintain separate queues for different resource-intensive operations
- Example: Scraping queue (I/O bound) vs Audio generation queue (GPU bound)
- Prevent resource contention by limiting concurrent jobs per queue
- Track running jobs separately per queue type

**Job Lifecycle:**
- `PENDING` → `RUNNING` → `COMPLETED`/`FAILED`
- Support `SUPERSEDED` status for jobs replaced by newer versions
- Persist job state to disk for recovery after server restart
- Filter out `SUPERSEDED` jobs from UI displays

### Subprocess Management

**Live Output Streaming:**
- Combine `stdout` and `stderr` for unified error reporting
- Use `bufsize=1` for line buffering (real-time updates)
- Stream output in separate thread (`asyncio.to_thread`) to avoid blocking event loop
- Update job messages in real-time as subprocess produces output

**Error Handling:**
- Capture up to 2000 characters of combined output for failed jobs
- Include exit code in error messages
- Log full tracebacks for debugging
- Provide actionable error messages in UI

**Example Pattern:**
```python
process = subprocess.Popen(
    cmd,
    stdout=subprocess.PIPE,
    stderr=subprocess.STDOUT,  # Combine streams
    bufsize=1,  # Line buffering
    text=True
)

# Stream output in background thread
async def read_output():
    for line in process.stdout:
        job['message'] = line.strip()
        self._save_jobs()
```

### Metadata Refresh After Jobs

**Post-Job Metadata Updates:**
- Always refresh metadata after job completion (file system may have changed)
- Re-run analysis functions (e.g., chunking) to get accurate positions
- Update both completed and pending item statuses
- Preserve historical metadata (generation times, created dates) when refreshing

**Idempotent Operations:**
- Use deterministic IDs for chunks/items (hash of content + position)
- Check file existence before marking as completed
- Support regeneration of failed items without duplicating successful ones

---

## API Design Patterns

### FastAPI Route Ordering

**Critical:** Specific routes MUST come before generic parameterized routes.

**❌ WRONG:**
```python
@router.get("/api/books/{book_id}")  # This will match "preview"!
async def get_book(book_id: str):
    ...

@router.get("/api/books/preview")  # Never reached!
async def get_preview():
    ...
```

**✅ CORRECT:**
```python
@router.get("/api/books/preview")  # Specific route first
async def get_preview():
    ...

@router.get("/api/books/{book_id}")  # Generic route after
async def get_book(book_id: str):
    ...
```

**Rule:** FastAPI matches routes in order. More specific routes must be defined first.

### Error Response Format

**Consistent Error Structure:**
- Return structured error objects with `error` or `message` field
- Include HTTP status codes appropriately
- Provide context for debugging (without exposing sensitive data)
- Log server-side errors with full details

---

## TTS-Specific Constraints & Patterns

### Character Limits

**XTTS v2 Constraint:**
- Hard limit: 250 characters per text segment
- Must enforce at chunking level, not just generation level
- Split paragraphs → sentences → words if necessary to respect limit
- Document limits clearly in code constants

**Chunking Strategy:**
1. First attempt: Split at paragraph breaks
2. If paragraph > limit: Split at sentence boundaries
3. If sentence > limit: Split at word boundaries (last resort)
4. Never exceed limit, even if it means single-word chunks

### Chunk Metadata Tracking

**Required Metadata Fields:**
- `text_start`: Character position in original text
- `text_end`: Character position in original text
- `status`: `'completed'` | `'pending'` | `'flagged'`
- `generation_time_seconds`: For performance tracking
- `created_at`: Timestamp for sorting/filtering
- `index`: Sequential chunk number (1-based)

**Metadata Refresh Logic:**
- Generate metadata for ALL planned chunks (completed + pending)
- Check file existence to determine status
- Preserve historical data (times, dates) for completed chunks
- Update counts based on completed chunks only

### Voice Registry Management

**Path Resolution:**
- Resolve relative paths against project root, not config file location
- Validate voice sample files exist before use
- Provide fallback/default voice if specified voice not found
- Log warnings for missing voice files (don't fail silently)

