## Quick Reference

### Must-Haves for Every Project

- [ ] Comprehensive `Makefile` (setup, teardown, rebuild, check-system)
- [ ] Metrics tracking infrastructure
- [ ] Golden dataset for testing
- [ ] Automated test suite (90%+ coverage)
- [ ] CI/CD pipeline
- [ ] Clear documentation (README, SETUP, architecture)
- [ ] `.gitignore` with credentials excluded
- [ ] `.env.example` template
- [ ] Validation before documentation
- [ ] Phase completion checklists
- [ ] Proper cleanup of intervals/polling in frontend
- [ ] URL state management for navigation persistence
- [ ] Background job queue management (separate queues for resource types)

### Red Flags

- ❌ No tests
- ❌ No metrics
- ❌ Documentation without validation
- ❌ Credentials in git
- ❌ Manual setup steps that could be automated
- ❌ No teardown/cleanup
- ❌ Vague success criteria
- ❌ No baseline comparisons
- ❌ Untested code in production
- ❌ Polling intervals not cleaned up (memory leaks)
- ❌ Generic API routes before specific routes (FastAPI)
- ❌ Hard-coded character limits without constants
- ❌ Missing metadata refresh after background jobs complete
- ❌ Modals/panels accumulating in DOM without cleanup

---

**Remember:** These are guidelines, not laws. Apply judgment based on project context, but document exceptions and reasoning.

